"it's a bird, baby" by infinite/@thatmarklee
---------------
"Imagine a an infant lying in its cradle and the window is open and into the room comes something marvelous, mysterious, glittering, shedding light of many colors, movement, sound, a transformative hierophany of integrated perception and the child is enthralled. 

And then the mother comes into the room and she says to the child 'That's a bird, baby. That's a bird.' Instantly the complex wave of the angel peacock iridescent transformative mystery is collapsed into the word. All mystery is gone. 

The child learns this is a bird, this is a bird. And by the time we’re five or six years old all the mystery of reality has been carefully tiled over with words."
-- Terence McKenna

--  
Uses p5js (LGPL-2.1). Color palettes are inspired by the paintings of Mondrian, Rafael, Van Gogh, Munch, O'Keefe, and Magritte.